Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T11:35:37-07:00","id":1387767,"title":"","content":"The new Shahan-Ya has a city with Waspfolk raiders in the South.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T11:53:59-07:00","id":1387769,"title":"","content":"I love the art, but looking at him, I get the sense that Ma-Ha-Suchi may be biting back a comment about the penmanship of the scroll he's holding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T12:10:53-07:00","id":1387773,"title":"","content":"This cover is really good. By far the best one of 3e books, to me.<br /> It's Great! I love it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1920-kim","name":"Kim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T12:29:27-07:00","id":1387783,"title":"","content":"Still not a fan of the fuzzy-one-person covers in 3e, but most of the art in the book is really solid. Overall, the book looks good","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/776-saintedphysician","name":"SaintedPhysician","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T13:07:56-07:00","id":1387790,"title":"","content":"I don't like the choice for the front style, but of the three, this one I like the most.<br /> <br /> And there's lots of art of cool shapeshifter brutality. Overall, while Exalted still doesn't have the best art in the rpg world, I think it's fairly good. Much improved from the Core.<br /> <br /> Other new charms:<br /> Silver Collar Binding gives people you've used Insidious Lunar Transformation social penalties against you.<br /> Devourer of Form is a pinnacle charm to reflexively use Insidious Lunar Transformation on anyone whose form you take without killing them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T13:21:09-07:00","id":1387793,"title":"","content":"There's a short tree of acting charms in Manipulation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T13:21:29-07:00","id":1387794,"title":"","content":"As a cover, I don't know, but that's entirely about whether these sort of covers are the best. That's a nice piece of art and clean graphic design. <br /> <br /> (I *do* kind of like that I know we'll look at cover guy's styling in ten years - or fewer - and be like &quot;Yep, that was definitely the '10s!&quot; about as much as we can look at Harmonious Jade on 1e's cover and be like &quot;Definitely the '90s!&quot;. Undercut+natural hair+big square beard! He's all subtly &quot;I'm Lunar in a very restrained a-more-mature-sound&quot; way, and not a Strength of Many &quot;Heck your mortal norms! My legs are a goat!&quot; way!).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T13:41:37-07:00","id":1387799,"title":"","content":"So, with Devourer of Form in Mind, I would like to direct everyone's attention to Blood Geas Binding. <br /> <br /> Aka &quot;Break this oath and you are now a pig&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T14:39:01-07:00","id":1387809,"title":"","content":"I was really hoping that Moon in Well Emanation would become totemic in Intelligence and/or there\u2019d be a few charms that would get that tag, but nope. Still just the one Totemic Intelligence charm and no \u201cI can create a spirit\u201d charm in Intelligence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T16:19:54-07:00","id":1387829,"title":"","content":"The quality of the cover-art is good, but I'm not impressed with the choice to represent the Lunar Exalted.<br /> <br /> The guy looks good and cool, but what about him gets across &quot;Here Be Werewolves&quot;?<br /> <br /> The cover of the second manual was better for this purpose, even if I feel the art wasn't as good as this art.<br /> <br /> I think there should be a big werebeast in the center, surrounded by a menagerie of beasts. Birds overhead, an elephant standing behind, rodents underfoot, a breaching whale in the background, and with Lunars in a variety of human forms mixed among them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T16:23:00-07:00","id":1387830,"title":"","content":"Page 114 allows you to create elder Lunars. Has anyone got any ideas for powerhouses ready to stomp over the Realm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T16:35:31-07:00","id":1387832,"title":"","content":"It's still only Lunars who've been exalted 20 or 30 years, not really Elders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T16:39:34-07:00","id":1387834,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure &quot;Grizzled Veterans&quot; are quite at &quot;Elder&quot; tier. They're only essence 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T16:58:29-07:00","id":1387837,"title":"","content":"Well, I guess it's finally time to retire the Google Drive document tab that has been featured on my browser for the last several months. It has served me well.<br /> <br /> Still, it does get to have one last hurrah in the form of being consulted to check on a certain language revision.<br /> <br /> Namely, under the Blessed Transformation header, I personally think that the current language about the Lunar relationship with gender identity is superior to the old version, both for better phrasing its concept of what shapeshifting can do for one's sense of that, acknowledgement of those who still deeply feel their gender identity, and using less encompassing terms on either count.<br /> <br /> Still, I never did find the time to ask a trans person what they thought about that concept within fiction in general and for Lunars in particular, so I still find my outlook on the subject to be limited. All I can say is that it's something that I feel more comfortable with.<br /> <br /> Hmm, might as well skip ahead and see what changes, if any, were made to descriptions of the Solar Bond. For the sake of balance.<br /> <br /> Ehhh a statement that most Solars who have a mate experience the same Tie formation, but it's not as all-encompassing because their Essence doesn't quite have that function of change, as well as there being Solars who would have never had a mate at all, I find those acceptable. Straightforward in being less one-sided, while still lending just a bit more of the force of the Bond in the Lunars direction to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T17:13:19-07:00","id":1387838,"title":"","content":"The picture of Jade and her Lunar buddy is really bad. It's like her face melted. Also Arianna isn't usually a brunette.<br /> <br /> Otherwise I like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8877-mrfamiliar","name":"MrFamiliar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T17:45:25-07:00","id":1387845,"title":"","content":"It's kinda funny how the whole book's style and illustrations really nails the epic artistic feel which permeates 3e... and then there's pages 81 and 277 with <b><i>AROOO </i></b>Cartoon werepeople.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T18:00:57-07:00","id":1387848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1387829#post1387829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The guy looks good and cool, but what about him gets across &quot;Here Be Werewolves&quot;?<br /> <br /> I think there should be a big werebeast in the center, surrounded by a menagerie of beasts. Birds overhead, an elephant standing behind, rodents underfoot, a breaching whale in the background, and with Lunars in a variety of human forms mixed among them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get where you're coming from. And your example could've been a cool way to do it.<br /> <br /> But I have to disagree with you on this.<br /> Seeing the cover art, the look of solemn determination, the glowing markings, the sword being drawn; all this tells a story in just one still image (something that would catch my interest, were I a stranger to the line), then turning the page and reading the phrase &quot;Fangs at the Gate&quot;, was a really pleasant experience to me. The juxtaposition of the art and that phrase is really evocative.<br /> <br /> The first part gives us a the protagonist; we see a person, we see that they're engaged in some sort of struggle or purpose both physically and mentally.<br /> The second part gives us the antagonist; what that purpose and struggle is directed against: &quot;the Gate&quot;, someting much larger than any one person, something that is representative of a larger concept. Something intangible. Faceless.<br /> Not something you can defeat in battle, with a slash of the sword. But drawing the sword is more symbolic in this case. The struggle is larger than any of us. But it has to be fought. And the fight must start somewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1920-kim","name":"Kim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T18:01:41-07:00","id":1387849,"title":"","content":"so everybody got theirs? I still havn't gotten the link from backerkit to get mine","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T18:04:53-07:00","id":1387850,"title":"","content":"I got two emails with it in. I'd just log in and look for it if I were you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T18:07:42-07:00","id":1387851,"title":"","content":"I did. they say I have no account. and so I tried getting the survey email again, and while they say they sent it, nothing arrived","signa