ecause Abyssals get necromancy, or no guy on the Sidereals cover because Avoidance Kata is a thing. If I want to convey that sense of \u201cHere Be Necromancers\u201d or \u201cHere Be Fate Bureaucrats,\u201d I have a whole book in which to do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T19:23:05-07:00","id":1387867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1387864#post1387864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally am glad that the cover character is not in Deadly Beastman Transformation; I would not want the chick on the Abyssals cover vomiting out a hungry ghost because Abyssals get necromancy, or no guy on the Sidereals cover because Avoidance Kata is a thing. If I want to convey that sense of \u201cHere Be Necromancers\u201d or \u201cHere Be Fate Bureaucrats,\u201d I have a whole book in which to do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly cannot tell if you're being sarcastic.<br /> <br /> Could you explain this a bit further?<br /> <br /> I mean, obviously a cover without anyone on it is a bad idea, setting aside that's not the best way to represent Avoidance Kata, but where else are you going to get Fate Bureaucrats? A book focused on Yu-Shan?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T19:27:54-07:00","id":1387868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1387837#post1387837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, I never did find the time to ask a trans person what they thought about that concept within fiction in general and for Lunars in particular, so I still find my outlook on the subject to be limited. All I can say is that it's something that I feel more comfortable with.</div> </div> </div> </div>For what it's worth, I was around for some of the relevant discussion in the Discord server at the time, and without naming names (I don't feel like it's my business), a few of the relevant people thought the first version was over the top as well. That's anecdotal, of course. It'd be interesting to hear if they ever got any hard data on what the community at large thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11796-sergregness","name":"serGregness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11796_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T20:14:23-07:00","id":1387876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1387837#post1387837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Namely, under the Blessed Transformation header, I personally think that the current language about the Lunar relationship with gender identity is superior to the old version, both for better phrasing its concept of what shapeshifting can do for one's sense of that, acknowledgement of those who still deeply feel their gender identity, and using less encompassing terms on either count.<br /> <br /> Still, I never did find the time to ask a trans person what they thought about that concept within fiction in general and for Lunars in particular, so I still find my outlook on the subject to be limited. All I can say is that it's something that I feel more comfortable with.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Judging by the new group I'm with having been gushing over for a while today they seem to be taking it favorably in my experience. (Many happy cry emojis)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T20:32:03-07:00","id":1387881,"title":"","content":"Trans people I have shown the book to, or told of the Blessed Transformation material, were quite happy with it, which I was glad to see. I didn't hear anyone object to the old wording, but that's just in my bubble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T20:36:56-07:00","id":1387883,"title":"","content":"Ok. Got things cleared uo.<br /> <br /> <br /> Off to read","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T22:16:40-07:00","id":1387905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1387867#post1387867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly cannot tell if you're being sarcastic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Consider the possibility that I am not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1387867#post1387867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you explain this a bit further?</div> </div> </div> </div>Gladly. <br /> <br /> The Solar on the Ex3 core cover is not Wyld Shaping. He is not using Brawl Charms to wrestle a gorilla, or using Resistance Charms to break the weapon of an attacker. That\u2019s in the book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1387867#post1387867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">where else are you going to get Fate Bureaucrats?</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Inside</b> the Sidereal book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T23:08:44-07:00","id":1387920,"title":"","content":"I'm sad that at this point it seems like there will never be even an optional-rules nod to people like me who hate the Tell as both a thematic and a mechanic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/563-roadie","name":"Roadie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar563_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T23:18:18-07:00","id":1387925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roadie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1387920#post1387920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sad that at this point it seems like there will never be even an optional-rules nod to people like me who hate the Tell as both a thematic and a mechanic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn\u2019t there that one charm in App that is basically \u201cignore all mechanics of your Tell until you go blazing\u201d?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T23:22:38-07:00","id":1387927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1387925#post1387925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn\u2019t there that one charm in App that is basically \u201cignore all mechanics of your Tell until you go blazing\u201d?</div> </div> </div> </div>If anything, that Charm actually annoys me more, because it makes it blatant that there was no actual central need for the Tell in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/563-roadie","name":"Roadie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar563_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T23:36:03-07:00","id":1387931,"title":"","content":"Just wanted to see if what I am seeing is right... that one can now have up to 16 dots in mutations with which to build Hybrid/War forms... 6 from Hybrid Body Transformation, 6 more from Beast-Form Empowerment and finally 4 more from Terrifying Ogre Alteration. This of course doesn't include any mutations one buys with merit dots or bonus points (during character creation) or experience points (during play)... just from the charms they have access to.<br /> <br /> I'm guessing this is to balance out the extra 6 dots that could be attained by taking Chimera-Soul Expression that allowed Lunars to gain additional mutations by taking on a second spirit-shape (like Ma-Ha-Suchi). It did seem a little unbalanced that Lunars with two spirit-shapes could have 6 more dots of mutations than Lunars with a single spirit-shape. That the mutations taken with these charms are exclusive (you can only express one set per activation of HBT), it does seem that this was meant to balance this discrepancy. My only question now is if Shifting Beast Nature also interacts with Chimera-Soul Expression (it specifically mentions Beast-Form Empowerment). I'm inclined to believe so as it is meant to create an alternate expression of mutations of one's hybrid form, which both CSE and BFE enhance.<br /> <br /> Did anyone else notice the implication of what was said in the Necromancy sidebar on page 310... that Lunars now have a natural affinity for Necromancy that makes them equal to the Solars in this practice with only the Abyssals surpassing them? Assuming that when Necromancy will follow a similar layout as it has in previous editions (3 circles), this suggests that Lunars will have access to 1st and 2nd Circles of Necromancy, just like Solars have had in past editions. If true, this will be a significant increase to their power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T23:44:43-07:00","id":1387933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1387931#post1387931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just wanted to see if what I am seeing is right... that one can now have up to 16 dots in mutations with which to build Hybrid/War forms... 6 from Hybrid Body Transformation, 6 more from Beast-Form Empowerment and finally 4 more from Terrifying Ogre Alteration. This of course doesn't include any mutations one buys with merit dots or bonus points (during character creation) or experience points (during play)... just from the charms they have access to.<br /> <br /> I'm guessing this is to balance out the extra 6 dots that could be attained by taking Chimera-Soul Expression that allowed Lunars to gain additional mutations by taking on a second spirit-shape (like Ma-Ha-Suchi). It did seem a little unbalanced that Lunars with two spirit-shapes could have 6 more dots of mutations than Lunars with a single spirit-shape. That the mutations taken with these charms are exclusive (you can only express one set per activation of HBT), it does seem that this was meant to balance this discrepancy. My only question now is if Shifting Beast Nature also interacts with Chimera-Soul Expression (it specifically mentions Beast-Form Empowerment). I'm inclined to believe so as it is meant to create an alternate expression of mutations of one's hybrid form, which both CSE and BFE enhance.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s probably correct, if I understand right. You either have your HBT + CSE or BFE mutations and you can choose to use Shifting Beast nature if you want.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Did anyone else notice the implication of what was said in the Necromancy sidebar on page 310... that Lunars now have a natural affinity for Necromancy that makes them equal to the Solars in this practice with only the Abyssals surpassing them? Assuming that when Necromancy will follow a similar layout as it has in previous editions (3 circles), this suggests that Lunars will have access to 1st and 2nd Circles of Necromancy, just like Solars have had in past editions. If true, this will be a significant increase to their power. </div> </div> </div>The Devs have said that that\u2019s been in the cards for yonks (it means that if you pair Sorcery+Necromancy practitioners together, Lunars are probably better than Sids, who only get 1st circle necromancy)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T00:31:28-07:00","id":1387943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roadie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1387927#post1387927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If anything, that Charm actually annoys me more, because it makes it blatant that there was no actual central need for the Tell in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Tell exists more for flavor than as an actual restriction for Lunars (because the Lunars are inspired in part by strange witches and other creatures in folklore who would always be recognizable by a distinctive trait).<br /> <br /> Unless your campaign is 100% about disguises (e.g. you're pretending you're the Scarlet Empress to take control of the Realm), it doesn't really break anything to just houserule it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T00:40:01-07:00","id":1387946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1387931#post1387931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...<br /> <br /> Did anyone else notice the implication of what was said in the Necromancy sidebar on page 310... that Lunars now have a natural affinity for Necromancy that makes them equal to the Solars in this practice with only the Abyssals surpassing them? Assuming that when Necromancy will follow a similar layout as it has in previous editions (3 circles), this suggests that Lunars will have access to 1st and 2nd Circles of Necromancy, just like Solars have had in past editions. If true, this will be a significant increase to their power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunars had access to 2nd Circle Necromancy in other editions, right? I'm sure they had it in 2.5","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8877-mrfamiliar","name":"MrFamiliar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T01:47:45-07:00","id":1387953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrFamiliar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1387946#post1387946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lunars had access to 2nd Circle Necromancy in other editions, right? I'm sure they had it in 2.5</div> </div> </div> </div>THey only could do 1st Circle in 1e and 2e. The logic was that Basically &quot;Abyssals and Solars swap, Lunars and Sidereals always one Circle less than Solars&quot; I think. This is the first editiont they are canonically straight-up Solar peers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T01:54:27-07:00","id":1387954,"title":"","content":"Hello everyone ! <br /> <br /> I was so happy to see the front cover yesterday. Does anyone got some awesome Lunar illustration he is willing to share with us ? <br /> <br /> Thanks anyway !","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T02:31:13-07:00","id":1387961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Did anyone else notice the implication of what was said in the Necromancy sidebar on page 310... that Lunars now have a natural affinity for Necromancy that makes them equal to the Solars in this practice with only the Abyssals surpassing them? Assuming that when Necromancy will follow a similar layout as it has in previous editions (3 circles), this suggests that Lunars will have access to 1st and 2nd Circles of Necromancy, just like Solars have had in past editions. If true, this will be a significant increase to their power. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, back in 2nd edition I always thought 'if they are so adaptable shouldn't they just be able to adapt to underworld mojo to at least manage 2nd circle Necromancy? Maybe at least a charm that lets them swap them around so they choose to be necromancy 2 and sorcery 1?'. I also thought it would balance them better against sidereals since sidereals get 3rd tier martial arts while matching lunars at second tier sorcery and matching them at both only getting ground floor 1st tier necromancy in 2ED. So to balance it then they could make it Sidereals 3/2/1 and lunars 2/2/2, and then it turned out they did that thing for 3rd edition (well, as close as can be since now martial arts are no longer in a 3 tier system) and it was nice to see an idea that popped into my head as maybe something to do if I ever did any homebrewing is now a thing officially. The only downside is that my amazing lunar necromancer can't be used until we get some necromancy released and, last I checked, we were only getting snippets of necromancy until they get around to the the Abyssal splat book (which is behind exigents and sidereals if nothing has changed since I last checked in a few months ago)<br /> <br /> Edit: Well, there is always the sidebars suggested 'just use sorcery with spooky necromancy paint splashed on and some basic home brew to turn summoning demons/elementals into ghost summoning until we release more detailed info' suggestion I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 05-13-2020, 05:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T02:47:39-07:00","id":1387967,"title":"","content":"I always thought they should be decent at necromancy because rat/vulture/owl/bat/cat/dog necromancer seems like an obvious character idea, and should be supported.<br /> <br /> They do also have a few appropriate charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-13-2020, 07:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T03:40:37-07:00","id":1387972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1387954#post1387954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Po