ass=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KymmetheSeventh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1387974#post1387974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In regards to the Blessed Transformation section, I think the text in the first paragraph is a bit problematic. Lunars receiving a perfect and all-inclusive transformation at or before character generation means that their players are denied exploring a trans narrative in play. There is no opportunity to undertake an empowering journey of self-exploration and self-discovery if the entire problem is solved in the moment of Exaltation.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're transformed in accordance with how they feel about themselves.<br /> <br /> I would readily interpret that as being held off if it's still something that is being figured out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T05:12:18-07:00","id":1387988,"title":"","content":"well, since I skipped the manuscript version this is my first time reading through this one. Anyone interested in hearing my thoughts? Or are you all passed that after reading the text already?<br /> <br /> I will say for now, pg 36, good job to the artist who depicted a Tyrant Lizard accuratly <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T05:26:56-07:00","id":1387991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1387972#post1387972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Some images from the kickstarter emails so hopefully okay to share. If not, apologies and I'll delete.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Gah. Sorry. Giving up and posting links. Apologies.<br /> <br /> Lunar v Abyssal<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://ibb.co/kmrnmT2\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://i.ibb.co/hYn5YNF/Lunar-1.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://ibb.co/kmrnmT2\" target=\"_blank\"> Lunar-1 hosted at ImgBB </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://ibb.co/kmrnmT2\" target=\"_blank\"> https://ibb.co/kmrnmT2 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Image Lunar-1 in the Moss-reynholm&amp;#039;s images album </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Flight of Separation<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://ibb.co/6y6cV13\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://i.ibb.co/RgLGZBx/Lunar-2.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://ibb.co/6y6cV13\" target=\"_blank\"> Lunar-2 hosted at ImgBB </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://ibb.co/6y6cV13\" target=\"_blank\"> https://ibb.co/6y6cV13 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Image Lunar-2 in the Moss-reynholm&amp;#039;s images album </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Black Winter Boneyard \u2013 Northern Lunar Dominion<br /> <a href=\"https://ibb.co/7VS8ywn\" target=\"_blank\">https://ibb.co/7VS8ywn</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Really like the third one","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T05:41:17-07:00","id":1387992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1387988#post1387988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">well, since I skipped the manuscript version this is my first time reading through this one. Anyone interested in hearing my thoughts? Or are you all passed that after reading the text already?<br /> <br /> I will say for now, pg 36, good job to the artist who depicted a Tyrant Lizard accuratly <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be, for one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T05:52:07-07:00","id":1387996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1387986#post1387986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're transformed in accordance with how they feel about themselves.<br /> <br /> I would readily interpret that as being held off if it's still something that is being figured out.</div> </div> </div> </div>The text is really clear here:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A Lunar who experienced gender dysphoria or similar discomfort with her assigned birth gender finds her true form in the pure self-understanding of Exaltation. </div> </div> </div>Mind, trans people often struggle with gender dysphoria for <i>years </i>before they can even put a name to their feelings or discover that they're unhappy with their assigned gender. The wording used implies that, even if a Lunar was still struggling with nebulous feelings of dysphoria or discomfort that they hadn't yet figured out, the moment they Exalt some force (their Essence, or something) checks if they're trans or not and, if so, transforms them into a perfect body that aligns with their innermost nature and then fills them with joy and affirmation to let them know that this new form is right for them. The text seems to cut out the possibility of self-exploration in favor of a transcendent moment of epiphany where one's true nature is revealed. Based on what the trans people in my life (my sister, my SO) have told me, this doesn't describe anything resembling their journeys of self-discovery.<br /> <br /> The text seems weirdly absolute, and it's strange to me that word count is spent here telling players the kinds of stories that they aren't allowed to tell, rather than expanding the variety of possible Lunar narratives. Even a little change like starting the first paragraph with 'Some Lunars' would avoid making an absolute statement and removing potential stories. Expanding the possibilities of narratives (especially queer narratives) is, to me, more in line with 3e's policy of inclusivity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11619-kymmetheseventh","name":"KymmetheSeventh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T05:54:54-07:00","id":1387997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KymmetheSeventh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1387996#post1387996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The text is really clear here:<br /> <br /> <br /> Mind, trans people often struggle with gender dysphoria for <i>years </i>before they can even put a name to their feelings or discover that they're unhappy with their assigned gender. The wording used implies that, even if a Lunar was still struggling with nebulous feelings of dysphoria or discomfort that they hadn't yet figured out, the moment they Exalt some force (their Essence, or something) checks if they're trans or not and, if so, transforms them into a perfect body that aligns with their innermost nature and then fills them with joy and affirmation to let them know that this new form is right for them. The text seems to cut out the possibility of self-exploration in favor of a transcendent moment of epiphany where one's true nature is revealed. Based on what the trans people in my life (my sister, my SO) have told me, this doesn't describe anything resembling their journeys of self-discovery.<br /> <br /> The text seems weirdly absolute, and it's strange to me that word count is spent here telling players the kinds of stories that they aren't allowed to tell, rather than expanding the variety of possible Lunar narratives. Even a little change like starting the first paragraph with 'Some Lunars' would avoid making an absolute statement and removing potential stories. Expanding the possibilities of narratives (especially queer narratives) is, to me, more in line with 3e's policy of inclusivity.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I'm not the only one that found this paragraph strangely worded and going against a lot of the possible Lunar themes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T06:06:58-07:00","id":1388003,"title":"","content":"It seems like there's two camps of trans exalted fans here. Some of them think the fantasy of going &quot;poof. you now have the exact body you want&quot; is great. Some of them want to explore the narrative of transition and overcome the challenges in a more realistic and I guess cathartic fashion. <br /> <br /> Lunars are shapeshifters who can freely alter their appearance with a single charm, and also literally steal the forms of other people. They are <i>much </i>better suited to satisfying the first group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T06:12:20-07:00","id":1388006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1388003#post1388003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems like there's two camps of trans exalted fans here. Some of them think the fantasy of going &quot;poof. you now have the exact body you want&quot; is great. Some of them want to explore the narrative of transition and overcome the challenges in a more realistic and I guess cathartic fashion.<br /> <br /> Lunars are shapeshifters who can freely alter their appearance with a single charm, and also literally steal the forms of other people. They are <i>much </i>better suited to satisfying the first group.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the question is about wether or not the game is &quot;better suited for a certain kind of group&quot;. I think it's really about having such an absolute thematic statement in a game that has the place to to both, and with likely the same word count. Just give the options to the ST and player what they want it to be. I mean they are probably going to do whatever they want anyway, but I really found this statement out of place with the rest of the mentality of Exalted 3e edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T06:14:05-07:00","id":1388007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1388003#post1388003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems like there's two camps of trans exalted fans here. Some of them think the fantasy of going &quot;poof. you now have the exact body you want&quot; is great. Some of them want to explore the narrative of transition and overcome the challenges in a more realistic and I guess cathartic fashion.<br /> <br /> Lunars are shapeshifters who can freely alter their appearance with a single charm, and also literally steal the forms of other people. They are <i>much </i>better suited to satisfying the first group.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Honestly, I don't see that much satisfaction in using the Lunars to explore those themes, because they can casually change their apparence as much as they want. You can't get a realistic experience while interpreting something that consider things like gender and apparence at best something that can be changed depending on the situation, and at worst something completely irrelevant to their personality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25288-shapechanger","name":"Shapechanger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25288_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T06:18:44-07:00","id":1388008,"title":"","content":"I'm just going to quote how Vance addressed this in the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2?p=1387821#post1387821\">Ask the Devs</a> thread, since it can be hard to follow everything that goes on in that thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2?p=1387821#post1387821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the best way I can address it is to explain the thought process behind it. Many-Faced Moon Transformation offers Lunars very all-encompassing control over their physical forms, and it's available to every Lunar. My concern was that this might become a &quot;must-buy&quot; Charm for players of trans Lunars, particularly those for whom the rest of the Charm's capabilities aren't a good fit for their character concept and so would feel like they'd lost out on a Charm slot/experience points. Making that transformation an intrinsic aspect of Lunar Exaltation (and to be clear, it's not Luna who does it, but an expression of the Lunar's own shapeshifting) addressed that concern and dovetailed nicely with Ex3 establishing Luna as a patron of trans and nonbinary people. I can definitely understand wanting to play through your transition over the course of the game, and you should feel free to ignore that part of the book if it gets in the way of the stories you're trying to tell.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T06:22:15-07:00","id":1388009,"title":"","content":"I think Chausse and I are of one mind here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1388003#post1388003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems like there's two camps of trans exalted fans here. Some of them think the fantasy of going &quot;poof. you now have the exact body you want&quot; is great. Some of them want to explore the narrative of transition and overcome the challenges in a more realistic and I guess cathartic fashion.<br /> <br /> Lunars are shapeshifters who can freely alter their appearance with a single charm, and also literally steal the forms of other people. They are <i>much </i>better suited to satisfying the first group.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's an unfair characterization. I don't think Lunars should prioritize one particular type of trans story. As the Blessed Transformation subsection is written right now, is prioritizing one story at the total exclusion of other possible stories, and I don't think that's good.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shapechanger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1388007#post1388007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. Honestly, I don't see that much satisfaction in using the Lunars to explore those themes, because they can casually change their apparence as much as they want. You can't get a realistic experience while interpreting something that consider things like gender and apparence at best something that can be changed depending on the situation, and at worst something completely irrelevant to their personality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shapeshifters who can change their appearance as much as they want are a great vehicle for exploring trans themes! Lunars have the ultimate freedom to experiment and explore every possibility of gender and identity. They're fantastical magic shapeshifters, but that doesn't stop them from having stories grounded in human emotion. Also, you seem to be assuming that Lunars have a unified opinion about gender and appearance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11619-kymmetheseventh","name":"KymmetheSeventh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T06:26:29-07:00","id":1388010,"title":"","content":"If anything, I'd remove the bit about it only applying to lunars who were dysphoric as mortals and say that they <i>all</i> get idealised bodies when they exalt. I mean, it just makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T06:28:44-07:00","id":1388012,"title":"","content":"Eeeeh..... I would not like all Lunars to get idealised bodies.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd rather relax what their &quot;true form&quot; is.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T06:31:47-07:00","id":1388014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1388010#post1388010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If anything, I'd remove the bit about it only applying to lunars who were dysphoric as mortals and say that they <i>all</i> get idealised bodies when they exalt. I mean, it just makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm curious about what you mean by &quot;idealized&quot; body.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T06:33:59-07:00","id":1388015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1388010#post1388010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If anything, I'd remove the bit about it only applying to lunars who were dysphoric as mortals and say that they <i>all</i> get idealised bodies when they exalt. I mean, it just makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div> I actually played a Lunar (albeit only for a few sessions) who Exalted as a old man but came out of it a youth. It was less about some idealized self, though, and more about symbolically shedding of a lifetime of cruelty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T06:36:06-07:00","id":1388017,"title":"","content":"The ability to alter your appearance at will and assume the forms of other people does not contradict the search to find one's self and determine one's own identity. It allows you to perform that search in a fun and fantastical way, but it does not override a journey to reach an understanding of who you are and who you want to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11619-kymmetheseventh","name":"KymmetheSeventh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T06:37:28-07:00","id":1388019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KymmetheSeventh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1388009#post1388009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shapeshifters who can change their appearance as much as they want are a great vehicle for exploring trans themes! Lunars have the ultimate freedom to experiment and explore every possibility of gender and identity. They're fantastical magic shapeshifters, but that doesn't stop them from having stories grounded in human emotion. Also, you seem to be assuming that Lunars have a unified opinion about gender and appearance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, Lunars are extremely good to represent trans people. But you based your complaint on the fact that Lunars can't struggle with self-discovery because they are changed into their ideal body when the Exalt. How can they struggle like a real person when they can change their gender with a thought -and a Charm, of course-? Maybe I'm just ignorant on how trans people live this particular problem, but I would think that the struggle normal trans people experience is in not small part dictated by the fact that changing gender is <i>not trivial</i> at all. You can't just wake up one day and say 'no, I feel like a woman' and immediately change your gender down to every single component of your body.<br /> <br /> If a Lunar pre-exaltation experienced gender dysphoria and don't get changed when she exalted, what exactly stops her to immediately change her gender and appearance multiple times and see if they feel more comfortable in that form? That they need to buy a charm? That's no struggle at all.<br /> <br /> Edit.<br /> <br /> Ok, you more or less answered me with what you wrote over there. However, the text is vague enough that you can still have a Lunar not accepting the change immediately. Just because they change in the 'pure self-understanding of Exaltation' it doesn't mean that they have to accept the change immediately. A trans Lunar that continues to use her old form until she's finally ready to completely leave behind her old life is still a journey. Not the usual one, but you're a shapeshifter anyway. The normal way is still more or less screwed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25288,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25288-shapechanger","user":"Shapechanger","date":". 05-13-2020, 09:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25288-shapechanger","name":"Shapechanger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25288_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T06:39:28-07:00","id":1388020,"title":"","content":"I just mean their &quot;true&quot; self in the same sense that the gender thing happens, but with other types of body dysmorphia. <br /> <br /> Really, what lunars best lend themselves to is explorations of gender fluidity, I think. Cos by default you only get one base form (here defined as the form you take when you un-commit all motes) and so, what if that shifts? you might find yourself experimenting with Many Faced Moon a lot, or even developing custom charms to flip between a few defaults without needing to spend willpower all the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T06:40:22-07:00","id":1388021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KymmetheSeventh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1388017#post1388017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The ability to alter your appearance at will and assume the forms of other people does not contradict the search to find one's self and determine one's own identity. It allows you to perform that search in a fun and fantastical way, but it does not override a journey to reach an understanding of who you are and who you want to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, essentially, it's the fact that you immediatly switch your True Form, rather than do it later having tried out different forms?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T06:41:35-07:00","id":1388022,"title":"","content":"It also occurs to me that Many-Faced Moon Transformation is permanent, so you can use it in the first scene to permanently change your True Form's gender, age, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T06:44:07-07:00","id":1388024,"title":"","content":"Yeah, like Vance said, without the auto switch, it can just become a charm tax on trans characters.<br /> <br /> The problem isn't the paragraph. the problem is that even without it, this sort of narrative is undermined by <i>everything else lunars can do</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T06:46:02-07:00","id":1388025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1388021#post1388021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, essentially, it's the fact that you immediatly switch your True Form, rather than do it later having tried out different forms?</div> </div> </div> </div>As presented now, trans Lunars immediately assume their true, innermost self and know with 100% certainty that this form is who they were always meant to be. I have an issue with this being presented as universal for all trans Lunars, since it removes the possiblity of trans Lunars who struggle with who they are, undertake long journeys of self discovery, experiment with various genders identities, etc - which are valid trans experiences precluded by the text.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11619-kymmetheseventh","user":"KymmetheSeventh","date":". 05-13-2020, 09:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11619-kymmetheseventh","name":"KymmetheSeventh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T06:49:49-07:00","id":1388028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1388021#post1388021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, essentially, it's the fact that you immediatly switch your True Form, rather than do it later having tried out different forms?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm unsure what the problem is exactly, but I don't think it's &quot;You find your True Form immediately&quot;. I think it's more about the fact that you expect that your character could have an inner journey to find out what he wants and why he wants it. But the phrasing &quot;You have the True Form you always wanted even if you didn't know what it was and you are happy now&quot; is telling the character what he feels now period. And it does seem contradictory with this idea of a possible inner journey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T07:03:55-07:00","id":1388034,"title":"","content":"I mean I guess you could have a lunar who looks at themselves after exaltation and goes &quot;My true self looks like <i>this</i>?&quot; but that's probably an indication of other self-image issues. <br /> <br /> &quot;You have the soul of a twink&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I don't want to be a twink. I want to be a big bara muscle dude&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T07:04:58-07:00","id":1388036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KymmetheSeventh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1388025#post1388025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As presented now, trans Lunars immediately assume their true, innermost self and know with 100% certainty that this form is who they were always meant to be. I have an issue with this being presented as universal for all trans Lunars, since it removes the possiblity of trans Lunars who struggle with who they are, undertake long journeys of self discovery, experiment with various genders identities, etc - which are valid trans experiences precluded by the text.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just for curiosity, how would you play a Lunar in a self-discovery of themselves? How much time do you think it's realistic for a Lunar to stay in a determinate gender before she understands what's the right one?<br /> <br /> I mean, considering that changing gender is so easy for them, the process doesn't look like it would require a lot of time, to begin with. Unless, of course, the Lunar is very, very confused, and doesn't have a set gender by default, but in that case there nothing changes from the text.<br /> <br /> Also, what stops a Lunar to try and change her gender identity even with this new certainty? The text doesn't preclude that. It also does not say the Lunar has to accept the transformation right away. Just because they know the new form is the right one, it doesn't mean that they're ready to leave behind the old one that easily. Or at least, the text does not suggest that they're brainwashed to automatically be at ease with the new form, even if they understand it's the right one. They could also second-guess the knowledge granted by the Exaltation, thinking it's something wrong about it and wanting to be sure.<br /> <br /> Basically, I think you're overthinking what was just a way for the Dev to have trans Lunar without having to buy a charm to play one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25288-shapechanger","name":"Shapechanger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25288_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T08:41:43-07:00","id":1388057,"title":"","content":"You can present concerns about the Blessed Transformation subsection using the errata form; it's not just for mechanics and typos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T10:36:25-07:00","id":1388087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1387988#post1387988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will say for now, pg 36, good job to the artist who depicted a Tyrant Lizard accuratly <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I <b>recognize</b> that Tyrant Lizard.<br /> <br /> Vance, is this illustration from <i>before </i>or <i>after </i>he taught the basics of economics to a herd of yeddim?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T12:22:11-07:00","id":1388115,"title":"","content":"Flowing Body Evasion has been changed to once per scene unless you reset by dodging 3 decisives, so now it's really just bad Seven Shadow Evasion. I wish they could have come up with some way for it to have a benefit.<br /> <br /> Edit: I guess it still has the advantage that the attacker resets to base which is nice if you survive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 05-13-2020, 03:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T12:26:52-07:00","id":1388119,"title":"","content":"Hmm, might be missing something but wanted to run it past people before listing it for the errata form. So page 100-101 mentions the Great Houses pulling back the legions, and the Black Lion was apparently ready to take the opportunity. Then we get these lines, that puzzle me, &quot;Just before the most recent, wildly successful offensive, the Dragon-Blooded abiding by the Pact\u2019s customs of hospitality. Even Third Daughter of the Leaves, for all that she\u2019s hardly spoken to another living soul since she seized Garianghis five years ago, has ordered her turtlewolves to admit sufficiently<br /> persistent Lunars to the city.&quot;<br /> <br /> The line about the hospitality doesn't seem to mesh into the Third Daughter of the Leaves bit. Like I'm guessing the DBs did something that amounted to a truce in some areas or something, but I'm not sure. Like I'm not alone right, it looks like there's something missing to other people?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T12:43:59-07:00","id":1388122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1388119#post1388119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, might be missing something but wanted to run it past people before listing it for the errata form. So page 100-101 mentions the Great Houses pulling back the legions, and the Black Lion was apparently ready to take the opportunity. Then we get these lines, that puzzle me, &quot;Just before the most recent, wildly successful offensive, the Dragon-Blooded abiding by the Pact\u2019s customs of hospitality. Even Third Daughter of the Leaves, for all that she\u2019s hardly spoken to another living soul since she seized Garianghis five years ago, has ordered her turtlewolves to admit sufficiently<br /> persistent Lunars to the city.&quot;<br /> <br /> The line about the hospitality doesn't seem to mesh into the Third Daughter of the Leaves bit. Like I'm guessing the DBs did something that amounted to a truce in some areas or something, but I'm not sure. Like I'm not alone right, it looks like there's something missing to other people?</div> </div> </div> </div>A whole chunk of text seems to have dropped out here. The text should read:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When the Great Houses called back the legions, Sha\u2019a Oka was ready to seize the moment. Just before the most recent, wildly successful offensive, the Dragon-Blooded controlled much of the pilgrimage road between the shrine cities, and at times all of it. Sha\u2019a Oka\u2019s offensive seized every city but Faxai, whose walls have endured for time out of mind. Between outcaste veterans, mercenaries, and martial orders, even the legions\u2019 absence hasn\u2019t wholly denuded the final shrine city\u2019s defenses.<br /> <br /> Each other shrine city harbors one of Sha\u2019a Oka\u2019s generals (p. XX). Some welcome guests to fight alongside them. Others prefer solitude, though grudgingly abiding by the Pact\u2019s customs of hospitality. Even Third Daughter of the Leaves, for all that she\u2019s hardly spoken to another living soul since she seized Garianghis five years ago, has ordered her turtlewolves to admit sufficiently persistent Lunars to the city. </div> </div> </div>If someone could put this into the errata form, that would be great. Thanks, and good catch!<br /> <br /> EDIT: My copy has the missing text, which is weird; it's on the top right-hand side of page 100. What do other people's copies look like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T13:05:53-07:00","id":1388126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1388122#post1388122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A whole chunk of text seems to have dropped out here. The text should read:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If someone could put this into the errata form, that would be great. Thanks, and good catch!<br /> <br /> EDIT: My copy has the missing text, which is weird; it's on the top right-hand side of page 100. What do other people's copies look like?</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, weird. I'll just list is as an error in my copy in case it was just a glitch in my download or something.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T13:07:16-07:00","id":1388127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1388122#post1388122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: My copy has the missing text, which is weird; it's on the top right-hand side of page 100. What do other people's copies look like?</div> </div> </div> </div>Has the missing text.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T13:24:09-07:00","id":1388134,"title":"","content":"Changes found:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Changes in the fluff :<br /> Raksi description of servering human flesh to guests of honor and being called out when she served a child to one of her apprentecies.<br /> There is a new fungus forest near Mahalanka.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Raksi has a new adherent; </span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Kerrich Storm-Favored - he's a hedonist</span></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Some new Lunar Dominions waspfolk in the south<br /> Sidebar about Necromancy and Solar Bond added,<br /> Sidebar about Giant proprortions added.<br /> Sidebar about talking animals and form taking charms added<br /> <br /> Lunar Chargen. Raising non favored/caste attributes for Lunars with caste are changed from 5bp to 4bp<br /> Carapace is changed, hypermobility and imposing features cost less.<br /> All Lunars now get 4 specialties at character gen, not 3.<br /> <br /> No Moons's shadow penumbra now gives enemies a -2 visual penalty to hit them.<br /> <br /> New Charms:<br /> Beast-Form Empowerment (buffs HBR)<br /> Silver Collar Binding (buffs Insidious Lunar Transformation)<br /> Devourer of Form (buffs Insidious Lunar Transformation)<br /> Soul\u2019s Eclipse Unity (better emotional connection to your Solar Mate)<br /> <br /> Charm changes in no particular order:<br /> Finding the Needle's Eye now just gives -1 Defence to the enemy instead of ignoring certain bonuses<br /> Striking Mospid Method rerolls higher of 3/Essence failures<br /> Relentless Lunar Fury 5m instead of 3m 1 wp<br /> Deathless Fury Unleashed changed to E3 and not having to be repurchased<br /> Unchained Monster Death-Rage added a second clause<br /> Halting the Scarlet Flow added out of combat clause<br /> Invincible Beast-Warrior Empowerment 8m 1 wp instead of 15m 1 wp, Perilous Keyword taken off, it also no longer applies to dice added by command actions<br /> Soul Beyond Shape is much cheaper.<br /> Mountainous Spirit Expression gets bonus soak/damage/lifting<br /> Glance-Oration Technique 3m instead of 4m<br /> Many-Voiced Mockingbird Attitude (mostly just clarifying) also totemic (Charisma)<br /> Angry Rhino Charge less prereqand also no mote cost to gain the initiative and the automatic success is taken out.<br /> Ox body two -2 and two -4s at stamina 5 instead of one -1 and one -2 and two -4<br /> Striking Mospid Method - rerolling higer of Essence or 3 failed dice , instead of Essence.<br /> Secret Sense Intuition: &quot;On a failed roll, the Lunar becomes aware only that someone is hidden nearby&quot; - is removed<br /> Flowing Body Evasion changed to once per scene with a reset function.<br /> Last Warrior's Unity has a damage nerf in tiny/miniscule forms.<br /> Moose soak and hardness nerfed.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> p.277<br /> Rampaging God-Beast Puissance is now simply God-Beast Puissance and costs 4m instead of 5m<br /> <br /> p.292<br /> Insidious Shadow Ruse has been folded into The Spider\u2019s Trapdoor<br /> <br /> Quicksilver Legend Evolution has gone from 15m, 1wp to 1wp","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-17-2020, 06:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T13:32:15-07:00","id":1388139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1387943#post1387943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Tell exists more for flavor than as an actual restriction for Lunars (because the Lunars are inspired in part by strange witches and other creatures in folklore who would always be recognizable by a distinctive trait).<br /> <br /> Unless your campaign is 100% about disguises (e.g. you're pretending you're the Scarlet Empress to take control of the Realm), it doesn't really break anything to just houserule it out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunars are far from the only shapeshifters in the setting to have that kind of feature, though. Bloody Hands have one hand that's exactly what their name suggests (and which can be only temporarily covered, as the blood eventually seeps out of any glove), Kireeki always has a bunch of tentacles, neomah always look like neomah versions of the subject, and Mara always has deer legs. Just shapeshifter stuff, as you do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T13:41:04-07:00","id":1388144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KymmetheSeventh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1387996#post1387996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The text is really clear here:<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I apologise. I allowed myself to slip into the usual mode of argument, which is far below the standards I think a topic such as this demands.<br /> <br /> The only thing that I want is for the presentation of the subject of gender with regards to Lunars to be better than it has been in past Editions. The question of how that is accomplished is ultimately... beyond me, but I'm happy for yourself and others to be driving a conversation about how it can be refined towards something more satisfactory around developers that are open to hearing it. I'm sorry for having not been more supportive.<br /> <br /> I truly hope that the final result does the best job that it can utilizing the medium to represent the nuances of the subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T13:43:17-07:00","id":1388146,"title":"","content":"I've got to say that the addition of a dramatic amount of extra text is truly intriguing and also... daunting. I'm not really sure what to do with it, heh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T16:49:06-07:00","id":1388183,"title":"","content":"I've just become aware of the fact that the wording for how Raksi welcomes political rivals has been changed to a form that more heavily implies that by the time people are being served on a platter, they're already dead (even if it at least gives the impression of a wider age range).<br /> <br /> I've got mixed feelings about this. On the one hand I liked the sense before that serving live babies was something so exaggerated that it made the idea that this was done as a psychological tactic more overt, even playful. On the other, I guess a point that definite murder is involved at least makes it more consistent with things like the Dragon Blooded vivisection.<br /> <br /> And I suppose that... it seemed unlikely that anybody who was served a baby would actually go through with it (but that does seem like it would more effectively serve the purpose of throwing them off balance and letting Raksi affect offence), whereas this form seems more accommodating to visitors that would hold their nose, close their eyes and stomach it, because at least they're not the actual killer and it's not as if refusal will bring them back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T16:58:44-07:00","id":1388187,"title":"","content":"Under shapeshifting &quot;She loses any mutations she possesses intrinsically (but not those granted by Charms)&quot; was changed to &quot;She loses any mutations she possesses intrinsically (but not those granted by magic)&quot;, so with time and sorcerous workings it seems you can stack mutations to your hearts content that will stay with you through different forms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 05-13-2020, 08:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T18:31:52-07:00","id":1388204,"title":"","content":"Songline Legend Runes has been renamed to Naming the World.<br /> <br /> Still requires you to commit 10m which feels like way to much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T20:42:05-07:00","id":1388223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1388139#post1388139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars are far from the only shapeshifters in the setting to have that kind of feature, though. Bloody Hands have one hand that's exactly what their name suggests (and which can be only temporarily covered, as the blood eventually seeps out of any glove), Kireeki always has a bunch of tentacles, neomah always look like neomah versions of the subject, and Mara always has deer legs. Just shapeshifter stuff, as you do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe a shapeshifter could have a Tell like Disney's version of Maui?<br /> <br /> No matter what form he takes, his face is always recognizably his own... somehow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T22:18:28-07:00","id":1388230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1388223#post1388223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe a shapeshifter could have a Tell like Disney's version of Maui?<br /> <br /> No matter what form he takes, his face is always recognizably his own... somehow.</div> </div> </div> </div>A quick YT jaunt later, and I'm torn between saying that it's mostly his eyes and smile, and that it might be a non-diegetic feature of the film to let the audience tell him apart from any other animal that might happen to be on the screen. In any case, 1e did that for Lunars, sort of, but assumed an entire wolf head, single cyclopean eye or the like - features that might seem monstrous, rather than &quot;hey, the face stays!&quot; or &quot;I don't even look like this person that I'm impersonating in the slightest and might as well be just lying about my identity to people who don't know any better, but no one seems to care!&quot;.<br /> <br /> Oh, sorry. The bitter tang surfaced a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T22:40:54-07:00","id":1388233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1388230#post1388230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A quick YT jaunt later, and I'm torn between saying that it's mostly his eyes and smile, and that it might be a non-diegetic feature of the film to let the audience tell him apart from any other animal that might happen to be on the screen. In any case, 1e did that for Lunars, sort of, but assumed an entire wolf head, single cyclopean eye or the like - features that might seem monstrous, rather than &quot;hey, the face stays!&quot; or &quot;I don't even look like this person that I'm impersonating in the slightest and might as well be just lying about my identity to people who don't know any better, but no one seems to care!&quot;.<br /> <br /> Oh, sorry. The bitter tang surfaced a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that is why you are supposed to sugar up the tang mix to taste before drinking it silly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T22:46:28-07:00","id":1388235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1388233#post1388233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well that is why you are supposed to sugar up the tang mix to taste before drinking it silly.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FX-OQFF_Frw\" target=\"_blank\">That's going to take a lot of sugar...</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T03:15:40-07:00","id":1388283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1388230#post1388230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A quick YT jaunt later, and I'm torn between saying that it's mostly his eyes and smile, and that it might be a non-diegetic feature of the film to let the audience tell him apart from any other animal that might happen to be on the screen.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only other animals that appear in the film are pigs and chickens, neither of which Maui turns into. He retains the facial expressions because it allows him to maintain character work.<br /> <br /> Heck, the actual pig in the film has a far more expressive face than real pigs are capable of.<br /> <br /> In any case, a Tell consisting of an animal managing to have recognisable expressions, even on a face that shouldn't be able to manage them, sounds right to me. After all, it's still a thing that requires sharp perceptions to properly recognise.<br /> <br /> Anyway, there's no need to relitigate one particular person's strong hangup about the Tell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T07:06:50-07:00","id":1388322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1388230#post1388230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;I don't even look like this person that I'm impersonating in the slightest and might as well be just lying about my identity to people who don't know any better, but no one seems to care!&quot;.<br /> <br /> Oh, sorry. The bitter tang surfaced a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Admittedly, I didn't think for a moment how it would impact shapeshifting into other human forms.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, &quot;magic&quot;. If people can ignore horns or inhuman eyes that their wife clearly didn't have before...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T13:36:33-07:00","id":1388415,"title":"","content":"I think of it as easier to picture as the Tell being legit not there visibly where it would logically make you fail to pass as whatever shape your in until the act of catching something off (someone hits the Perception roll) reveals it. That\u2019s how it\u2019s played in a lot of the inspirational fiction and folklore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 05-14-2020, 05:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T19:02:25-07:00","id":1388522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1388322#post1388322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Admittedly, I didn't think for a moment how it would impact shapeshifting into other human forms.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, &quot;magic&quot;. If people can ignore horns or inhuman eyes that their wife clearly didn't have before...</div> </div> </div> </div>The Tell explicitly hides from notice, or did. That's its magic, like a Solar with various Stealth Charms being invisible, inaudible, etc... until someone knows what it is, at which point it is glaring and sticks out to the observer when they start to suspect that something is amiss. In contrast, the other shapeshifters seem to be able to conceal their feature even if the witness knows what it is, at least to some extent; sussing out a bloody hand requires stalling for time, checking for deer legs on Mara might be socially unacceptable in a way that plays into her retaliating with Black Claw Style, and in any case, there's no &quot;you know this one's Tell, it is now super-obvious and cannot be concealed from you if the subject starts getting too weird&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T19:07:06-07:00","id":1388524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1388522#post1388522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Tell explicitly hides from notice, or did. That's its magic, like a Solar with various Stealth Charms being invisible, inaudible, etc... until someone knows what it is, at which point it is glaring and sticks out to the observer when they start to suspect that something is amiss. In contrast, the other shapeshifters seem to be able to conceal their feature even if the witness knows what it is, at least to some extent; sussing out a bloody hand requires stalling for time, checking for deer legs on Mara might be socially unacceptable in a way that plays into her retaliating with Black Claw Style, and in any case, there's no &quot;you know this one's Tell, it is now super-obvious and cannot be concealed from you if the subject starts getting too weird&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even someone who has seen a Tell before and knows 100% who you are still has to make the Difficulty 7 roll to notice it. They get 3 extra dice, but Difficulty 7 is still not what I would consider &quot;super obvious and cannot be concealed&quot;<br /> <br /> I mean, I would assume that not even all Exalts are masters of perceiving. (Note: Against anyone Trivial, apparently The Tell cannot be noticed at all. I.e. Even if your description of your Tell is plastered on warning posters across the entire city, anyone who does not warrant a stat block <i>will not notice</i> <i>it</i>)<br /> <br /> prototype00","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 05-14-2020, 10:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T19:15:20-07:00","id":1388527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1388524#post1388524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even someone who has seen a Tell before and knows 100% who you are still has to make the Difficulty 7 roll to notice it. They get 3 extra dice, but Difficulty 7 is still not what I would consider &quot;super obvious and cannot be concealed&quot;<br /> <br /> I mean, I would assume that not even all Exalts are masters of perceiving. (Note: Against anyone Trivial, apparently The Tell cannot be noticed at all. I.e. Even if your description of your Tell is plastered on warning posters across the entire city, anyone who does not warrant a stat block <i>will not notice</i> <i>it</i>)<br /> <br /> prototype00</div> </div> </div> </div>Apologies, was referring to past editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T19:16:27-07:00","id":1388528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1388527#post1388527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Apologies, was referring to past editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, then it is I who should apologize. Did not know that was what you were referring to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T19:36:29-07:00","id":1388536,"title":"","content":"I am curious as to whether my interpretation of Shapeshifting as written would be correct.<br /> <br /> In this case the rule that any mutations a character has are lost when in a form other than their natural one (or a beast-man form). For example, one concept I has was for a Lunar character with a Bat spirit shape to be blind, but use the Echolocation mutation to &quot;see&quot; (sort of like how Dare Devil or Toph Beifong does). There are of course limitations to this that allow for role-play moments (such as not seeing color or being able to read books and such). In human, bat-woman hybrid or spirit shape form, she would still be able to use this method to see... but if she took any other form, she would loose access to this mutation through such an interpretation of the rules as written, yes?<br /> <br /> I know I could get around this by tying her echolocation mutation to her Tell in some way (bat-like ears or an unusual voice perhaps), but given all the possible Tells (I was favoring unusual eyes to be honest), it seems a little punishing have this be my only options to keep the mutation in any form she takes. I know many STs would just hand wave this as it is core to the character's concept... but as written, this does seem to be the default (and an unusual voice does sound intriguing the more I think about it).<br /> <br /> Just curious as to see how many people agree that I have interpreted the as written ruling correctly and whether additional exceptions might need to be considered (or the rule scrapped all together).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T19:53:54-07:00","id":1388539,"title":"","content":"Your interpretation is Correct. The base game as written assumes that in any form that does not inherently have Echolocation, you will lose the benefits of the Echolocation mutation. <br /> <br /> Unless Tell (which you can flavour however you want really, it doesn\u2019t have to be Bat Ears, prominent forehead also works for a cetacean feel).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T21:27:30-07:00","id":1388556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1388536#post1388536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am curious as to whether my interpretation of Shapeshifting as written would be correct.<br /> <br /> In this case the rule that any mutations a character has are lost when in a form other than their natural one (or a beast-man form). For example, one concept I has was for a Lunar character with a Bat spirit shape to be blind, but use the Echolocation mutation to &quot;see&quot; (sort of like how Dare Devil or Toph Beifong does). There are of course limitations to this that allow for role-play moments (such as not seeing color or being able to read books and such). In human, bat-woman hybrid or spirit shape form, she would still be able to use this method to see... but if she took any other form, she would loose access to this mutation through such an interpretation of the rules as written, yes?<br /> <br /> I know I could get around this by tying her echolocation mutation to her Tell in some way (bat-like ears or an unusual voice perhaps), but given all the possible Tells (I was favoring unusual eyes to be honest), it seems a little punishing have this be my only options to keep the mutation in any form she takes. I know many STs would just hand wave this as it is core to the character's concept... but as written, this does seem to be the default (and an unusual voice does sound intriguing the more I think about it).<br /> <br /> Just curious as to see how many people agree that I have interpreted the as written ruling correctly and whether additional exceptions might need to be considered (or the rule scrapped all together).</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC, echo location also exists as a merit in the core book to represent people that just got good instead of having a form that gives them a racial bonus to listen checks and you don't lose those when shape shifted.<br /> <br /> Edit: Nope, I was wrong. But honestly I don't see why you can't just make it a merit in that vein in the name of your character concept, nothing says you are only allowed to make it a mutation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 05-15-2020, 12:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T21:38:03-07:00","id":1388558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1388556#post1388556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> IIRC, echo location also exists as a merit in the core book to represent people that just got good instead of having a form that gives them a racial bonus to listen checks and you don't lose those when shape shifted.<br /> <br /> Edit: Nope, I was wrong. But honestly I don't see why you can't just make it a merit in that vein in the name of your character concept, nothing says you are only allowed to make it a mutation.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I am aware, Echolocation only exists in the Lunars Splat:<br /> <br /> Echolocation (\u2022\u2022\u2022) \u2014 Innate<br /> Prerequisite: Enhanced Sense (Hearing)<br /> The mutant can \u201csee\u201d out to short range using hearing,<br /> ignoring penalties or increased difficulties due<br /> to blindness, darkness, poor visibility, etc. She can\u2019t<br /> discern color or fine detail, and solid obstructions like<br /> walls block echolocation.<br /> An alternative version of this mutation only functions<br /> while submerged in water but extends to medium range.<br /> <br /> You might be referring to Enhanced Sense in the Core<br /> <br /> Enhanced Sense (\u2022\u2022\u2022)\u2014Innate<br /> One of the character\u2019s senses becomes preternaturally<br /> acute, like that of a wild animal. The character adds two<br /> dice to all Perception rolls related to that sense.<br /> Drawback: This Merit is physically obvious in unusual eye<br /> color or shape, large ears, an elongated nose, or some other<br /> similar mutation.<br /> <br /> But that one, by the rules is not a mundane thing at all and has an attached drawback.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T02:21:09-07:00","id":1388612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1388536#post1388536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just curious as to see how many people agree that I have interpreted the as written ruling correctly and whether additional exceptions might need to be considered (or the rule scrapped all together).</div> </div> </div> </div> Your interpretation is correct, but the concept is still fully viable. Echo-Drinking Awareness, an Essence 1 Charm in the Perception: Senses tree, provides the exact effect you want in any form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T02:31:41-07:00","id":1388613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1388539#post1388539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your interpretation is Correct. The base game as written assumes that in any form that does not inherently have Echolocation, you will lose the benefits of the Echolocation mutation.<br /> <br /> Unless Tell (which you can flavour however you want really, it doesn\u2019t have to be Bat Ears, prominent forehead also works for a cetacean feel).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Considering the concept did include a bat spirit shape... bat-like ears did seem appropriate (hence why I suggested it), but you are right... if linked to a Tell I could flavor it anyway I see it. After some thought, an unusual voice is an interesting idea (another suggestion I made), thus using the Musical Voice and Echolocation mutations in combination sounds like it could be fun. Ma-Ha-Suchi has such a Tell (though no mutations related to it) after all. It would also be a good reason for this character to learn the Silver-Voiced Nightingale Style martial art.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T02:42:10-07:00","id":1388616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1388612#post1388612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Your interpretation is correct, but the concept is still fully viable. Echo-Drinking Awareness, an Essence 1 Charm in the Perception: Senses tree, provides the exact effect you want in any form.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh I know the charm exists... and the concept would likely have it, but relying on a charm to &quot;see&quot; in other forms can be problematic should there come a time when she can't use that charm (a rare situation to be sure, but still possible). Besides, this would be something she developed before she became a Lunar (thus before access to such a Charm).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T03:00:46-07:00","id":1388623,"title":"","content":"Well, she could have had the merit in her human form and then developed the charm when she exalted (and since its protean effect applies to mutations in human form, unlike most, it's not even redundant.)<br /> <br /> But on the other hand, having it be something she's been able to do since she was mortal makes it all the more viable to have as a tell. It does get around the 1 wp a day cost that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T18:03:09-07:00","id":1388804,"title":"","content":"That is exactly the way I was intending to go... especially since the Charm does provide a superior range at which she could see (out to Medium from Short). The main catch is that there may be times when she either can't or won't maintain the 5 mote and 1 willpower cost per day to keep the Charm active, but needs to make use of other shapes (or finds herself somehow locked into one of her other shapes). Such circumstances will admittedly be rare (as long as one's ST isn't a sadistic bastard), but I would still want to feel as if the character can still contribute in such situations without too many limitations (being unable to use shapeshifting due to the loss of &quot;sight&quot; would be limiting what she can potentially do).<br /> <br /> Tying this mutation to her Tell in some way does get around this and can make for a very interesting character.<br /> <br /> Still... i find it odd that beneficial mutations are treated in this way, while detrimental flaws are retained regardless of what shape one takes. Almost seems like a double standard to be honest. In the end... it doesn't really matter much... it simply is what it is whether or not I understand the why.<br /> <br /> I just wanted to make sure I understood the rules as written and what options I had to get around them (the rules that can not be broken can surely be bent, yes?).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T22:19:05-07:00","id":1388845,"title":"","content":"So, in terms of charm changes I just noticed that they made Soul Beyond Shape a lot cheaper, from 10 motes 3 willpower down to just costing 1 WP no motes at all. Guess they decided that permanently losing a shape was already a decently heavy cost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T00:59:49-07:00","id":1388860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1388845#post1388845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, in terms of charm changes I just noticed that they made Soul Beyond Shape a lot cheaper, from 10 motes 3 willpower down to just costing 1 WP no motes at all. Guess they decided that permanently losing a shape was already a decently heavy cost.</div> </div> </div> </div>My guess is it was buffed because a super costly cheat death doesn't really gel with 3e combat. 3e is all about going all out as much as you can, and every mote you do not spend is an edge you lose over the enemy.<br /> <br /> So a costly cheat death means either A - you won't be able to use the Charm when you need it. OR B - you have to hold back all the time to be sure you can use it, which means a Charm you bought to survive death is making you weaker at combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T02:03:22-07:00","id":1388867,"title":"","content":"Yeah, if you're being stabbed to death, there's a good chance you won't have 10 motes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T02:07:37-07:00","id":1388868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1388867#post1388867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, if you're being stabbed to death, there's a good chance you won't have 10 motes.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Can you stop for 20 seconds ? I need to check something real quick promise I won't escape&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T02:21:37-07:00","id":1388870,"title":"","content":"Edited the list on page 8 to include the cost reduction for Shape Beyond Soul","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T03:07:24-07:00","id":1388872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1388870#post1388870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edited the list on page 8 to include the cost reduction for Shape Beyond Soul</div> </div> </div> </div>Three more changes for the pile if of use:<br /> <br /> p.277<br /> Rampaging God-Beast Puissance is now simply God-Beast Puissance and costs 4m instead of 5m<br /> <br /> p.292<br /> Insidious Shadow Ruse has been folded into The Spider\u2019s Trapdoor<br /> <br /> Quicksilver Legend Evolution has gone from 15m, 1wp to 1wp","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T04:17:25-07:00","id":1388876,"title":"","content":"Thanks! I'll add those in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T08:53:10-07:00","id":1388957,"title":"","content":"While we're at it I haven't seen anyone point out that Selkie Mantle Endowment now gives mortals a dice cap of [Lunar's Essence] for any boosts they get from their animal form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T11:31:39-07:00","id":1389010,"title":"","content":"I should writeup a Lunar Dominion that is also one of the last surviving nations lead by the descendants of Loyalist Dragon-Blooded (I imagine those may have actually been relatively common Lunar allies during the Shogunate, but since they were in the Outer Threshold they took the brunt of the Fair Folk invasion, while the Shogunate had far heightened percentage of surviving heirs by virtue of the Sword taking out the Fair Folk before the Blessed Isle fell.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T12:07:04-07:00","id":1389026,"title":"","content":"Seems to me that part of what makes the Usurpation work is that once virtually all of the Solars are gone and you can be presumed to have no inkling of how to get them back, the difference between being a loyalist or not kind of becomes irrelevant. After about ten years... no, we'll be generous and say fifty years, the fact that you're in perpetual dispute with the government and your neighbours becomes indistinguishable from how the Shogunate on the whole works, you're just putting on some fancy airs about it.<br /> <br /> After a while, are there not more practical concerns for how you distribute loyalty?<br /> <br /> I imagine that for the most part, being Old Realm loyalist Dragon Blooded in the Shogunate played out like House Tepet as a Shogunate holdout in the Scarlet Dynasty; it gives you some identity that sets you apart, but doesn't change your need to participate in the prevailing system.<br /> <br /> Otherwise we get into a situation where there was and ever has been a bunch of Dragon Blooded with no identity beyond validating the presumed entitlement that Solars have to their loyalty. An entire nation of Risas, when just the one is already pushing their luck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T12:10:54-07:00","id":1389029,"title":"","content":"I can see it for twenty years. I can see it for 300, though probably at that point the House has been purged, and is a secret hidden house devoted to an ancient crackpot religion.<br /> <br /> But not really for 1500 years, through a massive 90% apocalypse. Or at least, by that time their myths and beliefs will have changed a lot so they worship Hesiesh the Sun God and believe the world was once ruled by Dragonblood priests of the sun, or some such.<br /> <br /> <i>But</i> I can see a Dragonblood loyalist house that gets purged, joins the Lunars, and basically turns into, well, a Lunar-supporting group of Dragonblood. Perhaps by then they're beastmen, or at least live out deep in the Threshold. I mean, New Dakuo supports the Vanguard, and they're only from the Shogunate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T12:36:43-07:00","id":1389037,"title":"","content":"Oh I forget to suggest that the point at which the prevailing attitude governing the world becomes that the Dragon Blooded are in charge, that's affording privileges even to the Terrestrials that claim to not want them, and that kind of establishes a pattern of behaviour that ultimately benefits the status quo.<br /> <br /> It makes me think of when Ireland was partitioned and they have the Unionist north home rule, which they'd never actually asked for and was technically contrary to their stated ideology, but having their own form of devolved government turned out to be so damn useful that they quickly adopted it as the default.<br /> <br /> Or for something less provincial, the manner in which the resolution of the American Civil War involved reintegration of the seceded state governments with relatively little in the way of reprisals or punishments.<br /> <br /> If there's nothing substantial for loyalists to fight for, it seems to me that the most practical solution is often to kill them with kindness. Let the inertia of their own position combined with the benefits of conformity render their opposition void.<br /> <br /> (Now to think of the counterexample of numerous regime changes that consolidated themselves with the extreme and violently ruthless removal of all past or present contrarians, out of the combination of it being part of the general milieu and the people in charge at least believing in the greater value of such purges, even if their reasoning was faulty.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T12:47:09-07:00","id":1389041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1389029#post1389029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>But</i> I can see a Dragonblood loyalist house that gets purged, joins the Lunars, and basically turns into, well, a Lunar-supporting group of Dragonblood. Perhaps by then they're beastmen, or at least live out deep in the Threshold. I mean, New Dakuo supports the Vanguard, and they're only from the Shogunate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I\u2019m wondering if New Dakuo has significant DB Beastfolk population.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T13:46:55-07:00","id":1389059,"title":"","content":"One Lunar Dominion that is on the map that I am surprised hasn't been mentioned outside of a single paragraph in the Exalted Book is the Broken Horn Tribe... between Ma-Ha-Suchi's nameless lair and where the ruins of Rathes has been moved to in 3E. From what I recall, they are mostly a thorn in the side of the nation of Nechara as they constantly raid the towns and trade caravans that pass through Nechara on the way to the Southeast. Beyond a mention of Lunar blood within the tribe, the Lunars that influence the tribe are interested in Nechara's genealogy records. That is all the information provided.<br /> <br /> There is no mention of it in Fangs at the Gate, and there doesn't seem to be mention of it in the rough outline we are given for Many-Faced Strangers (Lunar Companion). Maybe there will be mention of it in Across the Eight Directions, but at the moment it seems like an oversight (especially since I am thinking of using the area for a character's backstory and possible plot-hook).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T14:52:31-07:00","id":1389075,"title":"","content":"We just noticed that at bonfire, attacks against a No Moon take a -2 penalty. Was that the same before, or did it just say &quot;vision-based rolls&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T14:58:45-07:00","id":1389078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1389059#post1389059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no mention of it in Fangs at the Gate, and there doesn't seem to be mention of it in the rough outline we are given for Many-Faced Strangers (Lunar Companion). Maybe there will be mention of it in Across the Eight Directions, but at the moment it seems like an oversight (especially since I am thinking of using the area for a character's backstory and possible plot-hook).</div> </div> </div> </div> That just gives you freedom (not that I don't get the desire for more &quot;canon&quot; information).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1389075#post1389075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We just noticed that at bonfire, attacks against a No Moon take a -2 penalty. Was that the same before, or did it just say &quot;vision-based rolls&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div> It's a new thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T18:07:17-07:00","id":1389133,"title":"","content":"If it's really supposed to apply to regular attacks, what are full moons for?<br /> <br /> That's 2.0 dawns vs. twilights all over again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T18:17:05-07:00","id":1389134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1389133#post1389133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's really supposed to apply to regular attacks, what are full moons for?</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming you're talking about the -2 to hit No Moons, I think you're overstating the case here. Full Moons are still getting (Essence) non-charm dice on movement rolls and the higher of (Essence) or 3 natural soak, at the same anima level, plus getting to add (Attribute) non-charm dice to a Join Battle roll after landing a decisive, meaning they can very likely start at <i>considerably</i> higher initiative than just base, which No Moons have no comparable power for fighting. <br /> <br /> Plus, of course, there's the general thing that Full Moons aren't necessarily &quot;the fighty caste&quot;, the way Dawns are. Full Moons are &quot;the physical Attribute caste&quot;. That's a broader category than just fighting, and several other non-physical Attributes are also important for fighting, meaning that there's even less reason for Full Moons to be axiomatically better at fighting than every other Lunar.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T18:24:19-07:00","id":1389139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1389133#post1389133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's really supposed to apply to regular attacks, what are full moons for?<br /> <br /> That's 2.0 dawns vs. twilights all over again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not by half; in 2e, getting hit by any kind of attack <i>at all</i> was either death or the indicator of an inevitable slide into death. Given that getting hit by an attack is both more likely in this edition, <i>and</i> more survivable when it happens, I'd place more value on improving the ability to take a hit over improving the ability to not get hit, and that's before you factor in the movement bonuses and the higher Initiative Full Moons have after landing a decisive attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T18:46:58-07:00","id":1389151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1389133#post1389133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's really supposed to apply to regular attacks, what are full moons for?</div> </div> </div> </div>Getting in close and putting their hand through you.<br /> <br /> I'm being a bit reductive about even their combat capabilities there, but not half so much as you are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T18:54:12-07:00","id":1389156,"title":"","content":"Doesn't look like anyone mentioned it, but one change I noticed was that The Animorphs is now in inspirational reading.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure I'm the one who suggested that, so that's cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T22:41:35-07:00","id":1389201,"title":"","content":"That is indeed cool huh","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T23:14:29-07:00","id":1389206,"title":"","content":"If there\u2019s room to add anything to the list before release, KIPO and the Age of Wonderbeasts is amazing and works super well.<br /> <br /> i dare you to come up with a better Shahan-ya name than Yamyan Hammerpaw!<br /> <br /> And I can\u2019t help but imagine this song being song by Luna as a character is Exalting (potential inferred spoilers!): <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yxud2gUntQs\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yxud2gUntQs</a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T02:47:36-07:00","id":1389227,"title":"","content":"On No Moons and their anima:<br /> I'd like to point out that in 2nd ed they had an anima power that gave all attackers a -1 success penalty (so equivalent to 2 dice) on attacks against them.<br /> So this is nothing new.<br /> Also, they had a lot of combat charms favoured in Wits.<br /> <br /> And... yeah, the only person I ever saw play a No Moon was me, playing a sorcerer. I saw like 7 or 8 Full Moons.<br /> Believe me, an effective +1 Defence at bonfire, while good, isn't enough to get people to play &quot;combat No Moons&quot;, not when Full Moons get better access to combat charms, better access to starting physical attributes, soak bonus, combat movement bonus, and that amazing (if expensive) Join Battle power.<br /> <br /> It's not like 2.0 Twilights because a)the Twilight anima banner was amazing, and b)you had essentially as much access to combat abilities/powers as a Dawn.<br /> (I confess, I never saw a &quot;Combat Twilight&quot; but I did choose Twilight over Zenith for my first character partly because of the anima banner, and I regret it.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I agree with Kelly about Castes. Full Moons are the physical caste, which isn't quite the same as the combat caste.<br /> In my game, there's two Full Moons.<br /> Olaf Keelbreaker, the Steel Iceberg, is an absolute combat beast. Strength and Stamina 5, Melee 5 with a specialty in axes and a Grand Grimcleaver made from his own tusk, a whole bunch of attack-boosting charms, DBT, Mountainous Spirit Expression (which is now good), 3 ox-bodies, a bunch of soak charms, etc, etc.<br /> The other, Krove the Bull-Tiger, isn't bad at fighting per-se... he's got 8 dice for decisives, Parry 4, soak 7, one ox-body? But for a 100xp physical primary character, he's not amazing. Because he's all about being the strongest in all the land... not at combat, but at lifting things. I've seen him 20 successes to lift and throw menhirs. He resisted being grappled by the Elemental Dragon Mela. But he is definitely not a combat character, he's just okay at it coincidentally. I don't think he's really any better than the Changing Moon with a powerbow, or much better than the Casteless trickster with rapier or No Moon shaman with poisoned blowpipe. I'd say the Casteless king of the apes with Moonsilver Carapace and flaming fists is probably better.<br /> <br /> So I'm not bothered by other Castes being good at combat if it fits (for example, quick-witted No Moons or scary Changing Moons or genius tactician No Moons), as long as Full Moons are the fastest, strongest, nimblest and toughest. Similarly, I've got no real issue with a Full Moon blacksmith being a better smith than a No Moon due to her great strength, or a Changing Moon Joan of Arc who inspires her troops to fight much harder than the Full Moon's.<br /> <br /> Whereas if you go &quot;I want to play the best combatant/general&quot; with a Solar, it should be a Dawn. But then, your Dawn general might be Intelligence and Charisma 5 and physical tertiary, and that's fine. Similarly, your blacksmith might be a Supernal Crafter Twilight with Strength 5 and mental tertiary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T05:06:18-07:00","id":1389258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1389227#post1389227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Believe me, an effective +1 Defence at bonfire, while good, isn't enough to get people to play &amp;quot;combat No Moons&amp;quot;, not when Full Moons get better access to combat charms, better access to starting physical attributes, soak bonus, combat movement bonus, and that amazing (if expensive) Join Battle power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Among the things they're good at being that stealth.<br /> <br /> A thing that the No Moon who gets a little bit of extra defence while they're lit up like a Christmas tree would probably prefer when a Wyld Hunt is on the prowl.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T05:14:00-07:00","id":1389262,"title":"","content":"Actually, I'm pretty sure that a major difference between a power that imposes penalties on enemy attacks and a power like the Twilight one is that powers that eliminate your own penalties are easier than powers that reduce enemy defences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T06:23:39-07:00","id":1389288,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think there's a fair few Awareness charms that ignore visual penalties, so would ignore that.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T06:25:47-07:00","id":1389291,"title":"","content":"As would a blind character. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T06:27:46-07:00","id":1389293,"title":"","content":"Indeed.<br /> <br /> Or a character who closes their eyes and uses echolocation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T06:36:21-07:00","id":1389297,"title":"","content":"I honestly am way into the way the anima powers are. I really like the No Moon shadow-shroud, the fact that Changing Moons get bonuses to stealth and disguise while at dim anima, and the Full Moon fear-resistance. It reinforces Lunar flexibility in a way I'm pretty into.<br /> <br /> With No Moons specifically, I like that in some ways it incentivize blasting up to Bonfire---you're getting a defensive benefit while also (if you haven't used it already today) having the option to spend that anima on getting a WP back, juicing a spell up with motes, or a free full Excellency on a mental action (which might well be a spell's attack roll). Of course, once you do that, then you no longer have that free shadow-shroud until you get back up to Bonfire---and there's the obvious potential issue of attracting attention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T08:54:02-07:00","id":1389327,"title":"","content":"While I might have been a bit hasty posting my gut reaction and the two might be closer to tied when it comes to combat capability, I take issue with some of these arguments.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1389227#post1389227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Full Moons get better access to combat charms, better access to starting physical attributes</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, you can go Str/Dex/Per/Int as Favoured/Caste, Physical Primary, Mental Secondary as both full and no-moon and get the same charms and attributes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1389262#post1389262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I'm pretty sure that a major difference between a power that imposes penalties on enemy attacks and a power like the Twilight one is that powers that eliminate your own penalties are easier than powers that reduce enemy defences.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1389288#post1389288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I think there's a fair few Awareness charms that ignore visual penalties, so would ignore that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't think of any charms that let you ignore generalized attack penalties, and while DBs and Solars have some Awareness charms that let you ignore visual penalties on Awareness rolls you are generally not rolling attacks with Awareness.<br /> <br /> Even if you rule that they do apply on account of the rules for when charms can or can't apply to rolls with different abilities being a mess, that still leaves it a strong combat power against the vast majority of enemies who either arent' exalts or exalts that don't have those specific charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T09:16:24-07:00","id":1389332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1389327#post1389327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can't think of any charms that let you ignore generalized attack penalties</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh there aren't? Interesting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really, you can go Str/Dex/Per/Int as Favoured/Caste, Physical Primary, Mental Secondary as both full and no-moon and get the same charms and attributes.</div> </div> </div> </div>With only three Castes and nine Attributes, of which any given character is going to get four privileged, some stronger crossover between them than the other Exalted get might be kind of inevitable.<br /> <br /> Setting aside the question of whether that penalty measures up to what is provided by the Full Moon Anima, there's a question of whether or not that is a quality of the Lunar Exalted to lean into.<br /> <br /> Besides, the No Moon who tries acting more like a Full Moon is probably getting less Lunar XP, and so falling behind in the capabilities they buy up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T09:29:18-07:00","id":1389339,"title":"","content":"The DB Archery Excellency also removes one point of visual obstruction penalty for each added die, and beyond that there's the Aura effect of Feeling the Dragon's Bones (in Aura you get to commit the cost and keep the Charm up while Aura lasts). That's not negating generalized penalties, but it's certainly relevant to this specific example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8026,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","user":"Beans","date":". 05-17-2020, 12:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T09:51:15-07:00","id":1389345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beans</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1389339#post1389339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The DB Archery Excellency also removes one point of visual obstruction penalty for each added die, and beyond that there's the Aura effect of Feeling the Dragon's Bones (in Aura you get to commit the cost and keep the Charm up while Aura lasts). That's not negating generalized penalties, but it's certainly relevant to this specific example.</div> </div> </div> </div>The second archery charm for Solars also lets them completely ignore visual penalties to attacks.<br /> <br /> But that doesn't really matter. Comparing No to Full Moons and their combat abilities is comparing this:<br /> <br /> Full Moons<ul><li>Get two physical attributes favoured, being the only caste that can favour all three, or alternatively favour two and have flexibility favouring a mental and a social</li> <li>Gain a bonfire power of bonus (Essence or 3) soak, which stacks with armor, or for a turn for 5 motes.</li> <li>Gain a bonus (Essence) non-charm dice to all rolls to Rush, Disengage, vault a wall, tear down a tower, oppose an enemy rush, oppose an enemy disengage, etc.</li> <li>1/day when you make a decisive attack you can pay 10m 1wp to instead roll join battle with 5 non-charm bonus dice, which is killer.</li> </ul><br /> No Moons<ul><li>For 5 motes impose a -2 to hit penalty against most enemies for the turn, or free at bonfire.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> You might as well be saying that Full Moons are the OTB social build because they can add 3 non-charm resolve to any threaten rolls or fear based influence, for free, forever. Lunars are the most flexible of all the exalted anyway, if there's anyone you'd expect to be able to crossover a bit from one caste to another, it's Lunars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T09:53:47-07:00","id":1389348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1389327#post1389327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't think of any charms that let you ignore generalized attack penalties, and while DBs and Solars have some Awareness charms that let you ignore visual penalties on Awareness rolls you are generally not rolling attacks with Awareness.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Lunar anima power specifies that it's a visual penalty, and plenty of attack Abilities have charms to ignore those. Solars have Sight Without Eyes in Archery, Lunars have Sense-Sharpening Change and Heightened Sense Method in Perception, and Dragon-Blooded have Unobstructed Hunter's Aim in Archery (which is their Excellency, so it's quite basic). Also, the only restriction about using charms from other Abilities is that you can't generally activate them <i>when you're making a roll</i> with a given Ability. If a Solar has already activated Keen Sight Technique before making her attack, I'd certainly allow the bit about &quot;reduce the difficulty of seeing&quot; from visual hindrances to apply to the penalty. And I would allow Unsurpassed Taste and Smell Discipline and Unsurpassed Hearing and Touch Discipline to both function as &quot;targeting senses&quot;, within Close range at least, allowing someone who had them active to target enemies non-visually without penalty, getting around the Lunar anima power completely. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if you rule that they do apply on account of the rules for when charms can or can't apply to rolls with different abilities being a mess, that still leaves it a strong combat power against the vast majority of enemies who either arent' exalts or exalts that don't have those specific charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, it's a decent anima power, no argument there. But, again, the Full Moons aren't necessarily supposed to be the &quot;oops, all warriors!&quot; caste anyway, and they <i>still</i> have more, and better anima powers relating to combat. In 3e Exalted, having a good defense is nice in a fight, certainly, but it won't <i>win</i> you the fight either - you've got to be able to land hits of your own. Good defense alone is, at best, good for making it a no-score draw. If you took two Lunars, one a Full Moon and the other a No Moon, gave them no combat charms whatsoever, and equal investment in combat Abilities, I'd bet on the Full Moon every time, just based on anima abilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T10:30:57-07:00","id":1389356,"title":"","content":"I think the once-per-day power to roll Join Battle with non-Charm extra dice rather than reset to base power alone is a huge deal for Full Moon killing power, even with that cost.<br /> <br /> Thought about the Tell:<br /> <br /> Even with the notion that it has its own natural concealment, I feel as though the Tell goes along a bit with visual media in which somebody is shapeshifted, possessed or even just undergoing some personal issues which carry a visual element of ambiguous diegesis.<br /> <br /> Just as a way of picturing a scene in which a character is going around with sharper features and sideburns when they had none before, and nobody seems to notice until that key moment when somebody does (and puts it together that it indicates a shapeshifter). It's more satisfying to me than picturing it as something outright illusionary that melts away.<br /> <br /> Does it 100% make sense? No, but I feel as though modern readers have drifted away from the idea of something supernatural having qualities that don't quite flow logically. Like, don't even break down some specific mechanism to it, just embrace the idea that a shapeshifted Lunar can have a slightly compromised disguise that isn't actually compromised 90% of the time just because.<br /> <br /> Or if one must, think of it as just one little instance in which dealing with a Lunar is like engaging with something in a dream.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T23:36:16-07:00","id":1389579,"title":"","content":"It seems like the change to Jubilant Battle Proposition was missed, so I'll add it here. Just the part that was changed.<br /> <br /> Old text: The stylist catches foes off guard, concealing aggressive<br /> the intent behind joyous dancing. She Joins Battle with<br /> ([Appearance or Manipulation] + Performance), which<br /> also counts as a dance-based inspire roll against everyone<br /> who sees her,<u><b> ignoring penalties for multiple targets.</b></u><br /> <br /> <br /> New text: The stylist catches foes off guard, concealing aggressive<br /> the intent behind joyous dancing. She Joins Battle with<br /> ([Appearance or Manipulation] + Performance), which<br /> also counts as a dance-based inspire roll against everyone<br /> who sees her.<br /> <br /> Essentially, if you are not a Solar and cannot ignore the penalty for inspiring crowds with your excellency, you're stuck with the -'s on the influence roll, as I read it. Stealth mastery thing? Maybe it was missed on wordcount.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3575-dastardly_pug","name":"Dastardly_pug","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T00:52:24-07:00","id":1389587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dastardly_pug</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1389579#post1389579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems like the change to Jubilant Battle Proposition was missed, so I'll add it here. Just the part that was changed.<br /> <br /> Old text: The stylist catches foes off guard, concealing aggressive<br /> the intent behind joyous dancing. She Joins Battle with<br /> ([Appearance or Manipulation] + Performance), which<br /> also counts as a dance-based inspire roll against everyone<br /> who sees her,<u><b> ignoring penalties for multiple targets.</b></u><br /> <br /> <br /> New text: The stylist catches foes off guard, concealing aggressive<br /> the intent behind joyous dancing. She Joins Battle with<br /> ([Appearance or Manipulation] + Performance), which<br /> also counts as a dance-based inspire roll against everyone<br /> who sees her.<br /> <br /> Essentially, if you are not a Solar and cannot ignore the penalty for inspiring crowds with your excellency, you're stuck with the -'s on the influence roll, as I read it. Stealth mastery thing? Maybe it was missed on wordcount.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting, Lunars can ignore the penalty with Argent Songbird Voice (Cha), but thats a 2m surcharge.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T02:44:12-07:00","id":1389601,"title":"","content":"Hmm, Just realized that Chimera Soul expression has a mechanical edge on Beast form Empowerment because while both charms apply their mutations to HBT, only Chimera Soul Expression applies it to your animal spirit shape.<br /> <br /> On purpose or something for the errata form, you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T05:52:03-07:00","id":1389643,"title":"","content":"Probably mostly due to BFE being &quot;get more hybrid body at essence 1 without being a chimera&quot; first and foremost. You'd be applying mutations to a spirit shape based on... itself. <br /> <br /> But yeah, I was just thinking about this and maybe it would make more sense if it let you make &quot;pure&quot; hybrid forms of both animals if you're a chimera and pick between the three? Still not as good mechanically as chimera on its own but at least the two would synergise instead of being a nonbo.<br /> <br /> And maybe Shifting Beast Nature could be more flexible and let you make an alternate &quot;pure&quot; form or apply to both sets of mutations if you were a chimera, And maybe allow up to two repurchases to get alternate forms of the other two. <br /> <br /> This may be too many forms, idk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T05:57:32-07:00","id":1389644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1389643#post1389643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably mostly due to BFE being &quot;get more hybrid body at essence 1 without being a chimera&quot; first and foremost. You'd be applying mutations to a spirit shape based on... itself.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I was just thinking about this and maybe it would make more sense if it let you make &quot;pure&quot; hybrid forms of both animals if you're a chimera and pick between the three? Still not as good mechanically as chimera on its own but at least the two would synergise instead of being a nonbo.<br /> <br /> And maybe Shifting Beast Nature could be more flexible and let you make an alternate &quot;pure&quot; form or apply to both sets of mutations if you were a chimera, And maybe allow up to two repurchases to get alternate forms of the other two.<br /> <br /> This may be too many forms, idk.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, yeah, the mutations of Snake-Snake and Bear-Bear will probably be a bit hard to justify.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T07:17:10-07:00","id":1389655,"title":"","content":"I was surprised to see the small change in Ox Body Technique (stamina 5 no longer gets a -1 level, instead they receive an additional -2). Can someone speculate as to why that change was made?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T07:30:55-07:00","id":1389661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Apromor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1389655#post1389655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was surprised to see the small change in Ox Body Technique (stamina 5 no longer gets a -1 level, instead they receive an additional -2). Can someone speculate as to why that change was made?</div> </div> </div> </div>The scuttlebutt I've seen is that it makes the Berserker Charm Tree better (since you convert penalties to bonuses in that tree).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T07:42:25-07:00","id":1389666,"title":"","content":"It does make the Berzerker tree better, yeah. I just got 5 health levels turn from +1 to +2 in bear form!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T07:44:35-07:00","id":1389668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1389601#post1389601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, Just realized that Chimera Soul expression has a mechanical edge on Beast form Empowerment because while both charms apply their mutations to HBT, only Chimera Soul Expression applies it to your animal spirit shape.<br /> <br /> On purpose or something for the errata form, you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure it's intentional that becoming a chimera makes you a chimera.<br /> <br /> Yes, your hawk form now gets tentacles. But now your hawk form has tentacles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T12:24:08-07:00","id":1389726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dastardly_pug</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1389579#post1389579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems like the change to Jubilant Battle Proposition was missed, so I'll add it here. Just the part that was changed.<br /> <br /> Old text: The stylist catches foes off guard, concealing aggressive<br /> the intent behind joyous dancing. She Joins Battle with<br /> ([Appearance or Manipulation] + Performance), which<br /> also counts as a dance-based inspire roll against everyone<br /> who sees her,<u><b> ignoring penalties for multiple targets.</b></u><br /> <br /> <br /> New text: The stylist catches foes off guard, concealing aggressive<br /> the intent behind joyous dancing. She Joins Battle with<br /> ([Appearance or Manipulation] + Performance), which<br /> also counts as a dance-based inspire roll against everyone<br /> who sees her.<br /> <br /> Essentially, if you are not a Solar and cannot ignore the penalty for inspiring crowds with your excellency, you're stuck with the -'s on the influence roll, as I read it. Stealth mastery thing? Maybe it was missed on wordcount.</div> </div> </div> </div>Inspire rolls aren't subject to multiple target penalties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T17:52:14-07:00","id":1389801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1389644#post1389644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, yeah, the mutations of Snake-Snake and Bear-Bear will probably be a bit hard to justify.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, I asked the devs if you could be a chimerae of two subspecies of the same basic animal, and they said it was fine.<br /> <br /> Do you want to be both a venomous snake and a constrictor? You can do that.<br /> <br /> A poisonous arrowhead frog and a flying frog? You can do that.<br /> <br /> <br /> Remember the genetically engineered super-spider that bit Peter Parker in the first Sam Raimi movie? It was at least both a jumping spider and a web-weaving spider.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T18:07:45-07:00","id":1389803,"title":"","content":"Yeah but if you applied hybrid body transformations based on your (singular) spirit shape species <i>to </i>your spirit shape they wouldn't be two subspecies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T06:48:55-07:00","id":1389958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1389801#post1389801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah, I asked the devs if you could be a chimerae of two subspecies of the same basic animal, and they said it was fine.<br /> <br /> Do you want to be both a venomous snake and a constrictor? You can do that.<br /> <br /> A poisonous arrowhead frog and a flying frog? You can do that.<br /> <br /> <br /> Remember the genetically engineered super-spider that bit Peter Parker in the first Sam Raimi movie? It was at least both a jumping spider and a web-weaving spider.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe it was a 12 spider hybrid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 05-19-2020, 09:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T07:31:42-07:00","id":1389966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1389801#post1389801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah, I asked the devs if you could be a chimerae of two subspecies of the same basic animal, and they said it was fine.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It probably helps that those aren't differences in subspecies, but family. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Subspecies is when you take one of the several species of poison dart frog and distinguish it based on things like where they're found and slight variations in toe length or something.<br /> <br /> I'll admit that my initial instinct for the chimera would probably have been that it's based on distinctions that have more mythic recognition, but I can also see the value of recognising that a single order of a given animal can cover a pretty wide variety of types.<br /> <br /> &quot;Beetle&quot; is given as a single category of animal in the book, and yet I could imagine a Lunar chimera combining the mighty stag beetle (family <i>Lucanidae</i> consisting of around 1300 species) and the alluring firefly (family <i>Lampyridae</i> consisting of more than 2000 species).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T07:49:00-07:00","id":1389973,"title":"","content":"Subspecies is actually kind of vaguely defined. There are rules for them in the ICZN, but at least most biologists or philosophers of science who focus on this sort of thing don't treat them as much more htan convenient populations for humans to keep track of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T05:48:17-07:00","id":1391172,"title":"","content":"I reread the information on Tattoos on pages 134 and 135. I was under the impression that moonsilver tattoos would no longer prevent the Lunar from using invulnerable skin of bronze and similar magic. Yet looking at that section this isn't crystal clear. &quot;they render her immune ...to shaping effects inasmuch as they alter solely the body,<br /> such as a demon\u2019s petrifying gaze&quot; . Is this spelled out cleanly in another place?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T06:32:22-07:00","id":1391181,"title":"","content":"&quot;Shaping effects are any magic that transforms a character\u2019s body, mind, soul, or fate.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's not spelled out exactly, but the tatoos <i>have </i>to exclude effects that the lunar initiated themselves, or they wouldn't be able to shapeshift.<br /> <br /> Basically it's voluntary. They only work when the lunar wants them to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T06:54:34-07:00","id":1391184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Apromor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1391172#post1391172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I reread the information on Tattoos on pages 134 and 135. I was under the impression that moonsilver tattoos would no longer prevent the Lunar from using invulnerable skin of bronze and similar magic. Yet looking at that section this isn't crystal clear. &quot;they render her immune ...to shaping effects inasmuch as they alter solely the body,<br /> such as a demon\u2019s petrifying gaze&quot; . Is this spelled out cleanly in another place?</div> </div> </div> </div>It <i>is </i>specified, but weirdly only in the Lexicon section at the beginning of the book:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fangs At The Gate p.11</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>moonsilver tattoos:</b> Magical tattoos that Lunars use to choose their Castes and protect against unwanted magical transformation. Offered to Casteless Lunars by the Silver Pact</div> </div> </div> </div><i>unwanted </i>being the operative word here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T06:56:18-07:00","id":1391185,"title":"","content":"Something for the errata doc?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T07:03:18-07:00","id":1391188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1391185#post1391185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something for the errata doc?</div> </div> </div> </div>submitted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T16:10:24-07:00","id":1392690,"title":"","content":"Oh another change I haven't seen noted is Many-Faced Moon Transformation now allowing you to roll with [Int or Appearance] + [Larceny, Performance, or Presence] for disguises which is great for any pretty shapeshifters that aren't criminal geniuses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 05-29-2020, 09:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T21:13:44-07:00","id":1392748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1392690#post1392690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh another change I haven't seen noted is Many-Faced Moon Transformation now allowing you to roll with [Int or Appearance] + [Larceny, Performance, or Presence] for disguises which is great for any pretty shapeshifters that aren't criminal geniuses.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand it still disallows the disguise to be used for impersonation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T21:55:12-07:00","id":1392754,"title":"","content":"It would make all those hearts blood charms with all their requirements look a bit niche if you could just roll disguise with 20+ dice and no penalties for sex, ethnicity etc.to impersonate anyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T22:11:09-07:00","id":1392756,"title":"","content":"To be fair, getting those 20 dice takes quite a bit of a mote expenditure and a stunt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T17:40:13-07:00","id":1392952,"title":"","content":"Waiting two hours to get the motes back is orders of magnitude easier than f.ex. studying someone to find out a defining intimacy and then raising it to defining yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T22:11:24-07:00","id":1393003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>limaxophobiac</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1392952#post1392952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Waiting two hours to get the motes back is orders of magnitude easier than f.ex. studying someone to find out a defining intimacy and then raising it to defining yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree; how hard that would be depends entirely on what the Intimacy is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T17:34:04-07:00","id":1393263,"title":"","content":"Does the picture for Moon in Well Emanation on page 159 look a bit ...off to anyone else? I\u2019m honestly not sure if that Lunar is happy or grimacing in pain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T18:30:19-07:00","id":1393284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1393263#post1393263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the picture for Moon in Well Emanation on page 159 look a bit ...off to anyone else? I\u2019m honestly not sure if that Lunar is happy or grimacing in pain.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't like criticizing artists, I've tried to draw and while practice does lead to improvement I couldn't draw anything of nearly that quality without perhaps years of work..... but yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T19:18:42-07:00","id":1393295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1393263#post1393263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the picture for Moon in Well Emanation on page 159 look a bit ...off to anyone else? I\u2019m honestly not sure if that Lunar is happy or grimacing in pain.</div> </div> </div> </div>I interpret that image as the Lunar being the blue glowy one (she's the one with a caste mark after all), and the strange expression lady being the emanation.<br /> <br /> The Spirit has captured the Lunar's likeness at the exact moment the Charm was used, just moments ago. Now the Lunar watches as the spirit is slowly coming to life, kind of like a photograph being developed. Hence the frozen expression on the spirit's face.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T22:41:09-07:00","id":1393352,"title":"","content":"That is what happens when you are not very practiced at taking selfies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T04:15:24-07:00","id":1393390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1387676-fangs-at-the-gate-out-later-today-to-backers?p=1393295#post1393295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I interpret that image as the Lunar being the blue glowy one (she's the one with a caste mark after all), and the strange expression lady being the emanation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. After all, the Charm costs 20 motes, it seems uncommon to use it without some anima flaring.<br /> <br /> To me, that looks like an expression that says &quot;oh, I'm... alive. And for this purpose. Greeeeeeaaaatttt.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}